    "title": "U.S. Route 68 to close for six days starting Aug. 24 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Megan Southall ,\n4 hours ago\nXENIA, Ohio ( WDTN ) – U.S. Route 68 will be closed for six days beginning on Monday, Aug. 24, for work on the new pedestrian bridge at Great Council State Park as part of the shared-use path project.\nStarting at 8 a.m., U.S. Route 68 will be closed south of Bush Row Road until the end of the workday on Saturday, Aug. 29.\nWhile the road is closed, motorists will be detoured to S.R. 343, S.R. 72, and U.S. 42.\nCurrently, the U.S. 68 shared-use path project is on track to be completed by late October to early November, with final completion scheduled for early summer of 2027.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDTN.com.",
    "summary": "XENIA, Ohio ( WDTN ) – U.S. Route 68 will be closed for six days beginning on Monday, Aug. 24, for work on the new pedestrian bridge at Great Council State Park as part of the shared-use path project. Starting at 8 a.m., U.S. Route 68 will be closed south of Bush Row Road until the end of the workday on Saturday, Aug. 29. Currently, the U.S. 68 shared-use path project is on track to be completed by late October to early November, with final completion scheduled for early summer of 2027. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
